<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <RootNamespace>Test.Text</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>TestDependency</AssemblyName>

    <!-- NuGet package metadata -->
    <PackageId>TestDependency</PackageId>
    <Version>1.0.0</Version>
    <Authors>xxfast</Authors>
    <Description>
      The standing C# fixture library for the reverse bridge (C# to Kotlin), the mirror of
      what test-library is for the forward direction. Every reverse-direction feature
      (Phases 9–13) adds its fixture surface here, one feature-scoped namespace/type at a
      time, instead of hunting for a published package that fits the bridgeable subset.
      Keep each type within the subset the feature under test needs: no accidental overload
      sets, no constructs the ADR-043 filter would skip. Current surface:
      Test.Text.Template — static factory Parse(string) and static consumer
      Render(Template, string) (ADR-051, opaque handles); public instance constructor
      Template(string) (ADR-052); instance members Source (get), Name (get/set),
      Apply(string): string, and Clone(): Template (Phase 9 line 151).
      Test.Nullability.Nickname / NicknameBook / LegacyNicknameBook — nullable reference
      type annotations across return/parameter/property positions, plus a `#nullable disable`
      oblivious island (ADR-053, Phase 9 line 156/157).
      Test.Household.Toy / Cat / Household / StrayCat — the adversarial reverse fixture
      (ROADMAP "Tooling &amp; Test Integrity"): 3+ bound classes in one namespace, a
      cross-referencing settable handle-typed property (Cat.FavoriteToy : Toy), two types
      sharing a method name (Cat.Describe / Toy.Describe), a many-parameter method with a
      nullable annotated return (Household.FindToy), and a `#nullable disable` oblivious
      island whose method deliberately returns a genuine null (StrayCat.Announce).
      Test.Menagerie.IFeedable / ITagged / Ferret / Shy / TaggedFerret / Nocturnal /
      Sanctuary — ADR-070 fixture: a C#-declared interface surfacing in Kotlin as a Kotlin
      `interface` plus a handle-backed implementation, exercised at return, parameter and
      settable-nullable-property positions, an explicit-implementation negative case
      (Shy), an unbound-internal-runtime-type case (Nocturnal), interface inheritance
      (ITagged : IFeedable), and one interface per Decision 6 diagnostic (IBox&lt;T&gt;,
      IWithStatics, IWithDim, IIndexedThing, IEmpty).
      Test.Kennel.Kennel / Kitten, ADR-152 fixture (reverse Task / Task&lt;T&gt; to a Kotlin
      suspend fun): one member per seam, non-generic Task, Task&lt;int&gt; (no conversion),
      Task&lt;string&gt; and Task&lt;Kitten&gt; (conversion), Task&lt;string?&gt; (nullable),
      a fault after a real await, a synchronous throw before any Task exists, already-completed
      tasks (Task.FromResult / Task.CompletedTask), a static async method, ReadAsync beside a
      sync Read sibling (suffix kept), an async member taking a Kotlin-implementable IFeedable
      it uses AFTER the await, the single-byte NullableAttribute encoding (LedgerAsync), and one
      ValueTask&lt;int&gt; that must stay skipped with a named diagnostic.
      Test.Kennel.Kennel, ADR-153 additions (CancellationToken): a token-honouring member with
      observable C#-side state (StayAsync / StayCancelled / StayCancellations), a token-ignoring
      one (DawdleAsync), a `= default` token (DozeAsync), a token in a MID position beside a
      string and an int (FetchAsync), an already-completed token task (PounceAsync), the
      CallAsync() / CallAsync(CancellationToken) overload pair that folds to the token overload,
      two C#-side self-cancels (BoltAsync ending in TaskCanceledException, ScarperAsync in a user
      OperationCanceledException subclass), a sync OCE throw (Startle), and the two shapes that
      must stay skipped with info_cancellation_token_not_yet_mapped: a sync token-taking method
      (Wait) and a two-token one (HerdAsync).
      Test.Roster.ILabelled / Tag / Roster, ADR-155 fixture (BCL collections as eagerly copied
      Kotlin collections over a slot buffer): one member per mechanism, an int element (no
      conversion), a string element (one CoTaskMem slot each), a nullable element, a nullable
      collection, a map with a bit-cast double value, a set of a bound enum declared in another
      namespace, bound-interface elements (Labels), handle elements
      from a mutable declared type that must still bind read-only, a collection property
      (get/set), a collection constructor parameter, an IEnumerable&lt;string&gt; parameter, the
      Pick(IList&lt;int&gt;, Tag) / Pick(List&lt;int&gt;, ILabelled) overload pair that pins the
      shim's cast to the declared type, a lazy IEnumerable that throws mid-enumeration, the
      weak-reference AliveTags() collectability probe for element handles, and the shapes that
      must stay skipped with a named diagnostic: an array (Kennels), a struct element (Beds), and
      the AddRange(IEnumerable&lt;string&gt;) / AddRange(List&lt;string&gt;) pair that collapses to
      one Kotlin signature and is dropped as a whole set (skipped_overload_set).
</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    Re-pack command (run from the repo root, or from this directory):
      dotnet pack TestDependency/TestDependency.csproj -c Release -o test-library/build/nuget

    The output directory is the ADR-050 local feed referenced by the root nuget.config
    as "test-library/build/nuget".

    NOTE: test-library/build/nuget is a Gradle-generated output directory and is wiped
    by `./gradlew :test-library:clean :test-library:packNuget`. The build packs this
    fixture into that feed before packNuget (see the packTestDependency task in
    test-library/build.gradle.kts), so `dotnet restore` can resolve TestDependency.
  -->

</Project>
